From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] boards/rpi_4b: add Zephyr Dom0 board conf + overlay (BCM2711)

Add the Raspberry Pi 4 (BCM2711) counterpart of boards/rpi_5.{conf,overlay}.
Both are new files, so this patch adds nothing to the RPi5 board and the two can
coexist in one checkout.

The Zephyr-side fixes that patch 0008 root-caused on RPi5 hardware are folded
into rpi_4b.conf rather than re-derived: the raised shell/main/ISR stacks plus
HW_STACK_PROTECTION, MAX_XLAT_TABLES=32, LOG_MODE_IMMEDIATE, the 0x17 domctl
interface version with XENTROOPS_ARCH_* = n, and DISK_DRIVER_SDMMC=n with
FS_FATFS_WINDOW_ALIGNMENT=4 for an SD-less Dom0. None of them is BCM2712
specific.

Three things are genuinely different on BCM2711 and are commented in place:

* CELLS. boards/arm64/rpi_4b/rpi_4b.dts declares the root as 1/1 and
  dts/arm64/broadcom/bcm2711.dtsi does not give /soc its own cells, so /soc's
  children rely on the root's single address cell. bcm2712.dtsi declares
  #address-cells = <2> on /soc, which is why rpi_5.overlay can raise the root to
  2 cells. This overlay therefore keeps the root at 1/1 and writes single-cell
  addresses; everything it needs is below 4 GiB.

* CONSOLE. rpi_4b.dts points zephyr,console at &uart1, the BCM2711 aux/mini
  UART. Xen owns the console (boot.cmd passes dtuart=/soc/serial@7e201000, the
  pl011) and Xen's rpi4 platform blacklists the aux peripheral's page
  neighbours, so Dom0 uses the Xen PV console and &uart1 is disabled. No pl011
  node is added: the pinned Zephyr rev has none for BCM2711 and none is needed.

* SRAM RELINK to 0x20000000, derived rather than measured. Xen's rpi4 platform
  sets .dma_bitsize = 30, so allocate_memory_11() confines Dom0's bank[0] to
  below 1 GiB -- RPi5 has no platform entry, gets the 32-bit default and landed
  at 0xc0000000. With dom0_mem=256M (get_allocation_size gives exactly order 16)
  the only free naturally-aligned 256 MiB block under 1 GiB in the boot.cmd
  memory map is 0x20000000-0x30000000. rpi4-port/tools/check-memory-map.py
  recomputes this from the two files so it cannot drift silently.

The hypervisor node's grant-table base is likewise derived (find_gnttab_region()
uses __pa(_stext), i.e. boot.cmd's 0x02000000 Xen load address); its size and the
extended region still have to be confirmed against the first boot's Xen log, and
the exact log lines to read are quoted in the overlay.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/boards/rpi_4b.conf b/boards/rpi_4b.conf
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..de2a59d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/boards/rpi_4b.conf
@@ -0,0 +1,91 @@
+# Copyright (c) 2026 Yuichi Kusakabe
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+#
+# Zephyr Dom0 configuration for Raspberry Pi 4 Model B (BCM2711).
+#
+# Derived from boards/rpi_5.conf with patch 0008's hardware-verified fixes folded
+# in, because they were all root-caused on the Zephyr side and are not BCM2712
+# specific:
+#   - the raised shell/main/ISR stacks + HW_STACK_PROTECTION (xu create's domain
+#     build has large VLAs and overflowed a 4 KiB shell stack),
+#   - MAX_XLAT_TABLES=32 (arch/arm64/core/Kconfig:335 defaults to 8 for this board
+#     -- no USERSPACE and ARM64_VA_BITS=36 < 40, so neither the 12/16/20 branch
+#     applies -- and mapping a multi-MiB guest kernel exhausts 8),
+#   - LOG_MODE_IMMEDIATE (async logging interleaved with the shell on the shared
+#     Xen console made failure lines unreadable),
+#   - the 0x17 domctl interface version and XENTROOPS_ARCH_* = n for Xen 4.21,
+#   - DISK_DRIVER_SDMMC=n + FS_FATFS_WINDOW_ALIGNMENT=4 for an SD-less Dom0.
+#
+# RPi4-specific notes are marked [rpi4].
+
+CONFIG_XEN_DOM0=y
+
+CONFIG_XSTAT=y
+CONFIG_XSTAT_SHELL_CMDS=y
+
+# xu create runs on the shell thread and its domain build (load_modules ->
+# gen_domain_fdt) has large VLAs; 4 KiB overflowed and corrupted adjacent
+# .data/.bss on RPi5. HW_STACK_PROTECTION makes any residual overflow fault
+# cleanly with ELR/FAR instead of silently corrupting.
+CONFIG_SHELL_STACK_SIZE=32768
+
+CONFIG_MAIN_STACK_SIZE=16384
+CONFIG_ISR_STACK_SIZE=16384
+# NOTE: silently DROPPED by Kconfig on this board — it is absent from the built
+# zephyr/.config. Kept for the day the dependency is met; do not rely on it.
+CONFIG_HW_STACK_PROTECTION=y
+CONFIG_MAX_XLAT_TABLES=32
+
+CONFIG_XEN_VCH=y
+CONFIG_XEN_DOM0LESS_BOOT=y
+
+CONFIG_USE_DEFAULT_DOM_CFG=n
+CONFIG_DOM_CFG_BUILTIN_IMAGES=n
+
+CONFIG_DOM_STORAGE_FATFS_ENABLE=y
+
+CONFIG_FILE_SYSTEM_SHELL=y
+
+CONFIG_NOCACHE_MEMORY=y
+CONFIG_FS_MULTI_PARTITION=y
+CONFIG_DOM_STORAGE_FATFS_LOGICAL_DRIVE_NAME="1"
+# Guest images live in the FAT root of SD p1, not in a dom0/ subdirectory
+# (same as the RPi5 SoDeV build; patch 0002 makes that change for rpi_5.conf).
+CONFIG_DOM_STORAGE_FATFS_DIR=""
+CONFIG_XEN_LIBFDT=y
+
+CONFIG_DOM_CFG_LINUX_PV_DOMAIN=y
+
+CONFIG_XRUN_STORAGE_DMA_DEBOUNCE=4
+
+CONFIG_DOMU_MAX=5
+
+# Synchronous logging so a `xu create` failure line prints atomically on the
+# shared Xen console.
+CONFIG_LOG_MODE_IMMEDIATE=y
+
+# [rpi4] SD-less Dom0. boot.cmd.xen.zephyr-dom0.in marks
+# /emmc2bus/mmc@7e340000 xen,passthrough, so the SD controller belongs to DomD
+# (which owns the toolstack and serves the guest rootfs partitions over
+# virtio-blk). With its MMIO unmapped, an enabled SDHC controller would hang the
+# driver's SYS_INIT on the first register access and stop the init chain BEFORE
+# dom0less_init, so the dom0less DomD would never be introduced to xenstore.
+# rpi_4b.overlay therefore does not enable any SDHC node, and the disk driver is
+# turned off here so drivers/disk/sdmmc_subsys.c is not built against it.
+# FS_FATFS_WINDOW_ALIGNMENT is pinned because zephyr-dom0-xt/Kconfig defaults it
+# to SDHC_BUFFER_ALIGNMENT, which resolves empty once SDHC is inactive and breaks
+# the generated misc/generated/configs.c assembly.
+CONFIG_DISK_DRIVER_SDMMC=n
+CONFIG_FS_FATFS_WINDOW_ALIGNMENT=4
+
+# Xen 4.21 ABI. The two XENTROOPS_ARCH options add arm_sci_type (u16) and
+# vgsx_osid (u8) to xen_arch_domainconfig (16 -> 20 bytes) and grow
+# xen_domctl_getdomaininfo (120 -> 128 bytes); Xen 4.21 has neither field, so
+# leaving them =y mismatches getdomaininfolist.
+CONFIG_XEN_DOMCTL_INTERFACE_VERSION=0x17
+CONFIG_XEN_DOMCTL_XENTROOPS_ARCH_VGSX_OSID=n
+CONFIG_XEN_DOMCTL_XENTROOPS_ARCH_SCI_TYPE=n
+
+# SoDeV production guests (see src/dom_cfg/rpi_4b.c). Also settable from the
+# moulin builder vars in rpi4-sodev.yaml.
+CONFIG_DOM_CFG_SODEV=y
diff --git a/boards/rpi_4b.overlay b/boards/rpi_4b.overlay
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..494f965
--- /dev/null
+++ b/boards/rpi_4b.overlay
@@ -0,0 +1,148 @@
+/*
+ * Copyright (C) 2026 Yuichi Kusakabe
+ *
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+ *
+ * Zephyr Dom0 device-tree overlay for Raspberry Pi 4 Model B (BCM2711).
+ *
+ * Counterpart of boards/rpi_5.overlay. Three BCM2711 differences shape it:
+ *
+ *  1. CELLS. This overlay keeps the root at #address-cells = <1> /
+ *     #size-cells = <1> because every address it needs is below 4 GiB: the Dom0
+ *     bank is at 0x20000000 and the grant table at 0x02000000. That is a choice,
+ *     NOT a constraint — /soc gets its own #address-cells = <1> / #size-cells =
+ *     <1> from dts/arm64/armv8-a.dtsi:10-15, independently of the root, so its
+ *     children are unaffected by the root's cells and the root could be raised to
+ *     <2> exactly as rpi_5.overlay does (rpi_5.overlay:26-28) if a >4 GiB address
+ *     were ever needed here.
+ *
+ *  2. CONSOLE. rpi_4b.dts points zephyr,console at &uart1, the BCM2711 aux/mini
+ *     UART. Under Xen that UART is not Dom0's to use: Xen owns the console
+ *     (boot.cmd passes console=dtuart dtuart=/soc/serial@7e201000, the pl011) and
+ *     the aux peripheral's page neighbours are on Xen's rpi4 device blacklist.
+ *     Dom0 therefore talks over the Xen PV console, exactly as on RPi5, and the
+ *     board's UART is disabled. NOTE: no pl011 node is added — the pinned Zephyr
+ *     rev has none for BCM2711, and none is needed.
+ *
+ *  3. NO SDHC. The RPi4 SD controller (/emmc2bus/mmc@7e340000) is handed to DomD
+ *     by boot.cmd.xen.zephyr-dom0.in, and the pinned rpi_4b board does not define
+ *     an SDHC node at all — so unlike rpi_5.overlay there is nothing to disable
+ *     here. boards/rpi_4b.conf still sets CONFIG_DISK_DRIVER_SDMMC=n so the disk
+ *     driver is not built.
+ */
+
+/delete-node/ &sram0;
+
+#include <mem.h>
+
+/ {
+	chosen {
+		zephyr,console = &xen_consoleio_hvc;
+		zephyr,shell-uart = &xen_consoleio_hvc;
+	};
+
+	psci {
+		method = "hvc";
+	};
+
+	xen_consoleio_hvc: hvc {
+		compatible = "xen,hvc-consoleio";
+		status = "okay";
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * reg[0] = grant table, reg[1..N] = extended regions.
+	 *
+	 * Xen writes the real values into the domain device tree, but Zephyr
+	 * cannot parse them at runtime, so they are hard-coded here and MUST be
+	 * confirmed against the first boot's Xen log:
+	 *   (XEN) Grant table range: 0x............-0x............
+	 *   (XEN) d0: extended region 1: 0x..........->0x..........
+	 *
+	 * Derivation of the values below (see also
+	 * rpi4-port/meta-rpi5-sodev/meta-xt-common/meta-xt-dom0-zephyr/RPI4-PORT.md):
+	 *
+	 *   grant table: find_gnttab_region() in xen/arch/arm/domain_build.c sets
+	 *     gnttab_start = __pa(_stext), i.e. where boot.cmd loaded the Xen binary
+	 *     -> 0x02000000, and gnttab_size = gnttab_dom0_frames() << PAGE_SHIFT
+	 *     = min(gnttab_max_frames, PFN_DOWN(_etext - _stext)) frames. MEASURED
+	 *     from this build's xen-syms map: _stext 0xa0000200000, _etext
+	 *     0xa0000277978 -> 0x77978 = 0.47 MiB = 119 frames, so the real region is
+	 *     0x77000 (rpi_5 measured 0x7b000). 0x100000 over-declares ~2x, which is
+	 *     harmless; under-declaring is not. Earlier text here guessed "about 1 MiB".
+	 *
+	 *   extended region 1: find_unallocated_memory()
+	 *     (xen/common/device-tree/domain-build.c) does NOT report holes in the
+	 *     memory map. It seeds a rangeset from bootinfo_get_mem() — the RAM banks
+	 *     only — and then subtracts the assigned ones, so a physical range that is
+	 *     not RAM can never come out of it. The gpu_mem carve-out is exactly that,
+	 *     which is why this used to name 0x3b400000-0x40000000 and was wrong. The
+	 *     value below mirrors rpi_5.overlay's measured shape: the unallocated RAM
+	 *     above Xen and below DomD's lowest static-mem bank. Confirm from the log.
+	 */
+	hypervisor: hypervisor@2000000 {
+		compatible = "xen,xen";
+		reg = <0x02000000 0x100000>, <0x02200000 0x05e00000>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_PPI 0x0 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE IRQ_DEFAULT_PRIORITY>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&gic>;
+		status = "okay";
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * Dom0's direct-map RAM bank. Xen loads the Dom0 image at
+	 * bank[0].start + text_offset and cannot be told where to put it
+	 * (construct_hwdom -> allocate_memory_11 ignores xen,static-mem, which is a
+	 * dom0less-domU-only mechanism), while Zephyr is absolute-linked from
+	 * CONFIG_SRAM_BASE_ADDRESS, auto-derived from this node. A mismatch runs
+	 * garbage and faults before console init — on RPi5 the symptom was total UART
+	 * silence and no xu-create.
+	 *
+	 * 0x20000000 is derived, not copied from RPi5 (which uses 0xc0000000):
+	 *   - Xen's rpi4 platform sets .dma_bitsize = 30
+	 *     (xen/arch/arm/platforms/brcm-raspberry-pi.c), so allocate_memory_11()
+	 *     computes lowmem_bitsize = min(32, 30) = 30 and confines bank[0] to
+	 *     below 1 GiB. RPi5 has no platform entry, gets the 32-bit default, and
+	 *     therefore landed at 0xc0000000.
+	 *   - boot.cmd.xen.zephyr-dom0.in passes dom0_mem=128M, and
+	 *     get_allocation_size(128 MiB) is exactly order 15 = 128 MiB.
+	 *   - In that boot script's memory map the first free naturally-aligned
+	 *     128 MiB block below 1 GiB is 0x20000000: everything under it is taken
+	 *     (boot modules below 0x08000000, DomD static-mem bank1
+	 *     0x08000000-0x20000000), and the map deliberately leaves this hole.
+	 * rpi4-port/tools/check-memory-map.py recomputes this from the two files and
+	 * prints the expected address, so it cannot silently drift.
+	 *
+	 * SIZE IS 128 MiB, NOT 256 (changed 2026-08-04). dom0_mem used to be 256M,
+	 * but 256 MiB could never be satisfied as one block on this board: the
+	 * firmware places the host DT blob at 0x2eff1f00 (observed on hardware as
+	 * MODULE[1] 0x2eff1f00-0x2f000fff), which is inside 0x20000000-0x30000000,
+	 * so allocate_memory_11() halved the order and Dom0 actually received
+	 * 128 MiB @0x20000000 + 128 MiB @0x30000000 -- two banks with a hole between
+	 * them, while this node claimed one contiguous 256 MiB region. Zephyr would
+	 * have treated 0x28000000-0x30000000 as its own RAM and faulted on use.
+	 * Asking for 128M makes the request equal to the first bank, so the
+	 * declaration matches what Xen hands over, and it returns 128 MiB to the
+	 * guest budget -- which is what makes the 4 GiB three-domain cockpit fit.
+	 * Do NOT lower it further: the scan starts at address 0, so 64M matches
+	 * 0x04000000 and 32M matches 0x00000000, where config.txt's
+	 * armstub=bl31.bin (TF-A BL31 + the secondary-CPU spin tables) lives.
+	 *
+	 * CONFIRM on the first boot:
+	 *   (XEN) Allocating 1:1 mappings totalling 128MB for dom0:
+	 *   (XEN) BANK[0] 0x000020000000-0x000028000000 (128MB)
+	 *   (XEN) Loading zImage from 0x02400000 to 0x20000000-0x2.......
+	 */
+	sram0: memory@20000000 {
+		compatible = "mmio-sram";
+		reg = <0x20000000 DT_SIZE_M(128)>;
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * The BCM2711 aux/mini UART: Xen owns the console, Dom0 uses the PV console.
+ * Disabling it also keeps Dom0 away from the aux peripheral page that Xen's rpi4
+ * blacklist protects (brcm,bcm2835-aux / -aux-spi).
+ */
+&uart1 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
